  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 153 AM MDT Mon May 25 2026\n\nA low pressure system is expected to move onto the Pacific \nNorthwest coast tonight. The low will move through Oregon and \nstall over the western Great Basin by Wednesday. Then the low \nwill weaken and lift out towards the end of the week. \nSignificant widespread precipitation with this system is \nunlikely but isolated to scattered thunderstorms will be \npossible just about each day, especially during the afternoon. \nToday will be the warmest day with highs in the 70s across the \nmountains and highlands with mid to upper 80s for the Snake \nPlain and Magic Valley. Highs will cool some with upper 70s to \nlower 80s likely for the Magic Valley and Snake Plain for \nmidweek. As the low lifts through our area late week, highs will\ncool a little more with temps generally sitting around 70 for \nthe Magic Valley and Snake Plain. Frost/freeze still looks \nunlikely this week with temps in most lower elevations holding \nin the 40s for morning lows. &&",
